#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""CorridorKey 2.0 - windowed interface.

Layout (fits the window, no scrolling):
    header  : logo (spins while a job runs) + status
    body    : Setup & hint | Preview workspace | Outputs & GPU
    footer  : stopwatch, progress, Stop / Open folder / Run

It builds the same command the command-prompt launcher (run_interactive.py)
builds, runs infer.py in the background and shows the live log. Theme selection and advanced controls live in Preferences. Render GPU is preflighted before every job; if CUDA-enabled PyTorch is missing and an NVIDIA driver is present, the app can install its pinned GPU packages.

Start it with:  python CorridorKey_Studio.py (from the CorridorKey project folder)
Needs:          pip install customtkinter   (numpy, opencv, pillow are already
                in the project's requirements.txt)
"""
